  "tables": [],
  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Use the `if()` function in the expression of a matchmaking rule to return values depending on a Boolean conditional. For example, `if (true, `0.0`, `1.0`)` returns `0.0`, and `if (false, `0.0`, `1.0`)` returns `1.0`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Declaration",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "```swift\nany if(boolean $condition, any $ifTrue, any $ifFalse)\n```",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Parameters",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "-`condition`: An expression that evaluates to a Boolean value. -`ifTrue`: The value to return if `condition` is `true`. -`ifFalse`: The value to return if `condition` is `false`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Return value",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Returns `ifTrue` if `condition` is `true`; otherwise, `ifFalse`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    }
  ],
